    "description": "The Child Adolescent Bullying Scale (CABS) is a 40-item self-report questionnaire assessing bullying involvement — including perpetration, victimization, and bystander roles — in children and adolescents. It is used to evaluate the nature and extent of bullying experiences in school and peer contexts.",
